window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-katsuragi-kouhei"]=[{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p59-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"totsuka-yahiko sakayanagi-arisu ibuki-mio katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 2  2 3  the class a leader who showed his card a reinforced cave on the mountainside  he comes out and stands watch at the entrance  lectures his partner on the school s hints   the ship s deliberate circle around the island  the path visible from the deck    finding it was inevitable  be mindful of what you say and do  the chapter s model of class a thinking   before the ship docked at the pier  it had already taken a trip around the island as a detour for some reason  that was probably a deliberate move by the school to give the students some hints  named as the rival his partner expects to silence by holding the cave  the contempt line that frames class d   class d is just an assortment of failures  right  they re defective  considering the point difference  it s probably fine to ignore them  right    overruled as enough chit chat  identified by the watchers as class a s spot leader holding the key card   a mistake ayanokoji files as  a fatal mistake  for the seventh day guess rule","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3: the Class A leader who showed his card<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.59–62<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A reinforced cave on the mountainside; he comes out and stands watch at the entrance.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Lectures his partner on the school&#x27;s hints — the ship&#x27;s deliberate circle around the island, the path visible from the deck — &quot;Finding it was inevitable. Be mindful of what you say and do.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s model of Class A thinking: &quot;Before the ship docked at the pier, it had already taken a trip around…the island as a detour for some reason. That was probably a deliberate move by the school to give the students some hints.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Named as the rival his partner expects to silence by holding the cave.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The contempt line that frames Class D: &quot;Class D is just an assortment of failures, right? They’re defective. Considering the point difference, it’s probably fine to ignore them, right?&quot; — overruled as enough chit-chat.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Identified by the watchers as Class A&#x27;s spot-leader holding the key card — a mistake Ayanokōji files as &quot;a fatal mistake&quot; for the seventh-day guess rule.<span class=\"pg\">p.61–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the parley at the cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  3 4  the parley at the cave named first as absent from the class a cave  then arriving at the entrance midway through the standoff with horikita  the page introduces him as the sharp witted one of the pair who found the cave on the first day   what are you doing  i don t recall giving you permission to invite guests   well then  it should be fine for you to look inside  however  prepare yourself  the moment you touch anything  i will notify the school and report your actions as obstruction toward another class  i can t guarantee what will happen to class d as a result  threatens a school report over touched vinyl   read as probably bluffing  with some genuine danger behind it   you re right about that  i cannot argue the point  however  it s something of an unspoken rule  you in class d have a spot by the river  class b has a well  you live in and surround the occupied space  so it s halfway monopolized  have you taken any forceful measures in dealing with trespassers to your area  concedes the formal point and answers it with practice  every class already defends its own area   one class occupies one spot  then  they continue to protect that spot so they may obtain points until the end of the test  if you violate this unspoken rule  it creates chaos  naturally  class a will trespass upon class d s base in retaliation  we should avoid trouble  states the island s working rule  one spot per class  held for the whole test  or retaliation follows   we are quite capable  we also expect things from you  class d  by which i mean  your futile struggling  pulls his partner off the provocation  answer bait like that and the other side backs down  ends her advance with words  the narration has her stopped in her tracks by his calm  with him on the entrance  class d s only option is retreat   he has stripped every other one away","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.4: the parley at the cave<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.127–129<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named first as absent from the Class A cave, then arriving at the entrance midway through the standoff with Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What are you doing? I don’t recall giving you permission to invite guests.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well then, it should be fine for you to look inside. However, prepare yourself. The moment you touch anything, I will notify the school and report your actions as obstruction toward another class. I can’t guarantee what will…”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re right about that. I cannot argue the point. However, it’s something of an unspoken rule. You in Class D have a spot by the river. Class B has a well. You live in and surround the occupied space, so it’s halfway…”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The page introduces him as the sharp-witted one of the pair who found the cave on the first day.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, it should be fine for you to look inside. However, prepare yourself. The moment you touch anything, I will notify the school and report your actions as obstruction toward another class. I can’t guarantee what will happen to Class D as a result.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Threatens a school report over touched vinyl — read as probably bluffing, with some genuine danger behind it.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re right about that. I cannot argue the point. However, it’s something of an unspoken rule. You in Class D have a spot by the river. Class B has a well. You live in and surround the occupied space, so it’s halfway monopolized. Have you taken any forceful measures in dealing with trespassers to your area?”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Concedes the formal point and answers it with practice: every class already defends its own area.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “One class occupies one spot. Then, they continue to protect that spot so they may obtain points until the end of the test. If you violate this unspoken rule, it creates chaos. Naturally, Class A will trespass upon Class D’s base in retaliation. We should avoid trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> States the island&#x27;s working rule: one spot per class, held for the whole test, or retaliation follows.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We are quite capable. We also expect things from you, Class D. By which I mean, your futile struggling.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Pulls his partner off the provocation: answer bait like that and the other side backs down.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ends her advance with words; the narration has her stopped in her tracks by his calm.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> With him on the entrance, Class D&#x27;s only option is retreat — he has stripped every other one away.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p59-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the Class A leader who showed his card<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p140-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: the cornfield offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p140-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi totsuka-yahiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 4  4 3  the cornfield offer arrives with yahiko at the thicket while sakura is staring at the corn  apologizes for the surprise  apologizes for startling her   he has seen where she ran to behind his back   i m sorry  we didn t mean to surprise you  he had no bad intentions  either  please forgive us   my name s katsuragi  from class a  he s yahiko  since this is the second time we ve met  a self introduction should be fine  yes   you found this  don t worry  we have no intention of snatching it away from you  but if someone else finds this spot  they ll likely take it away   you re the one who doesn t seem to understand the situation  yahiko  don t dismiss the danger of moving through the forest alone  it s difficult enough in groups of men  but when men and women are together  no matter what  there will be certain limitations to what you can do  will not go into the forest alone   groups of men already strain  mixed company more  the narration gives it as the reason he never went alone   we ll help you   i see  we can t force you  however  can you trust us  after you leave here  there s a chance we ll make off with all of this  right  silences his objections with a look after the head thump  partnership is offered over his visible refusal  the offer and the trust question both land on him  he refuses the first and gives up the spot rather than accept the second  and katsuragi withdraws without force  offer refused  he pivots to asking to be trusted instead   then quietly clears a path for them  stays at the corn after they leave so their harvest runs under his eye  whether that was good or bad intent is left open  class a now knows the spot and watches it from close by","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.3: the cornfield offer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.140–142<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives with Yahiko at the thicket while Sakura is staring at the corn; apologizes for the surprise.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry. We didn’t mean to surprise you. He had no bad intentions, either. Please forgive us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“My name’s Katsuragi, from Class A. He’s Yahiko. Since this is the second time we’ve met, a self-introduction should be fine, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You found this. Don’t worry, we have no intention of snatching it away from you. But if someone else finds this spot, they’ll likely take it away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Apologizes for startling her — he has seen where she ran to behind his back.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re the one who doesn’t seem to understand the situation, Yahiko. Don’t dismiss the danger of moving through the forest alone. It’s difficult enough in groups of men, but when men and women are together, no matter what, there will be certain limitations to what you can do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Will not go into the forest alone — groups of men already strain, mixed company more; the narration gives it as the reason he never went alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ll help you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. We can’t force you. However, can you trust us? After you leave here, there’s a chance we’ll make off with all of this, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Silences his objections with a look after the head-thump; partnership is offered over his visible refusal.<span class=\"pg\">p.140–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The offer and the trust-question both land on him; he refuses the first and gives up the spot rather than accept the second, and Katsuragi withdraws without force.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Offer refused, he pivots to asking to be trusted instead — then quietly clears a path for them.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stays at the corn after they leave so their harvest runs under his eye; whether that was good or bad intent is left open.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class A now knows the spot and watches it from close by.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: the parley at the cave<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p198-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.4: the card in the memory<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p198-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 6  6 4  the card in the memory named from day one  ayanokoji tells horikita he saw katsuragi hold a card in front of the class a cave  the sighting is the cave moment from the volume s second chapter   his card  now weighed against horikita s   well  is this the same card that katsuragi kun had  he takes no part in the day s scenes  the chapter keeps him named only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p198-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.4: the card in the memory<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.198<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named from day one: Ayanokōji tells Horikita he saw Katsuragi hold a card in front of the Class A cave.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Well? Is this the same card that Katsuragi-kun had?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The sighting is the cave moment from the volume’s second chapter — his card, now weighed against Horikita’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He takes no part in the day’s scenes; the chapter keeps him named only.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p140-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.3: the cornfield offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p222-1\">→ After: Ch.6 §6.9: the handshake in the woods<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p222-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 6  6 9  the handshake in the woods steps out of the shadows at ryuen s call to inspect the stolen leader card under his own condition   it looks like the real thing  the narration frames him as calm and dependable   the complete opposite of class c s leader   and calls his caution near paranoid   you re right  the short assent carries no speaker tag  it sits under ryuen s pressure  before the narration notes he still has not consented   you bastard  why are you telling me this   sakayanagi is absent  it s impossible for someone indecisive to rule class a   we ve established negotiations  as promised  i accept your proposal  shakes his hand on the class c alliance   the narration calls it signing a contract with the devil  confirms her engraved card as real under the flashlight   the proof ryuuen set as his condition   i ll be heading back now  i don t want to risk things by lingering for too long  returns the card and disappears into the darkness  commits class a to an alliance with class c in ryuen s hands  in his rival s absence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 §6.9: the handshake in the woods<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.222–224<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Steps out of the shadows at Ryūen’s call to inspect the stolen leader card under his own condition.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It looks like the real thing,”<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You bastard. Why are you telling me this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration frames him as calm and dependable — the complete opposite of Class C’s leader — and calls his caution near-paranoid.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The short assent carries no speaker tag; it sits under Ryūen’s pressure, before the narration notes he still has not consented.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sakayanagi is absent. It’s impossible for someone indecisive to rule Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ve established negotiations, as promised. I accept your proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Shakes his hand on the Class C alliance — the narration calls it signing a contract with the devil.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Confirms her engraved card as real under the flashlight — the proof Ryuuen set as his condition.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll be heading back now. I don’t want to risk things by lingering for too long.”<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Returns the card and disappears into the darkness.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Commits Class A to an alliance with Class C in Ryūen’s hands, in his rival’s absence.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p198-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.4: the card in the memory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p244-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the strange result<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p244-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 7  the strange result muttering over the announced results on the beach  then named through the lounge retelling as the cautious holder of the class a cave  class a takes third with 120 points  behind class b s 140 and class d s 225   something is strange  what does this mean  the question follows the narration that he muttered it  recorded as his  the class a cry  what s the meaning of this  katsuragi  comes from unnamed voices and is left out as a chapter attribution gap  the one who read his cave display as insurance rather than carelessness   the leader beside him was yahiko  not him  totsuka yahiko was class a s leader  katsuragi only displayed the card while the two were at the cave  class a s internal schism is the reason katsuragi could not rely on other people   why the methods revealed class a so easily  the retelling s reading of his class  270 points at the end of the test  not one spent   bought through class c s sacrifice   and still third  ayanokoji s own label for it intuition with no evidence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p244-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the strange result<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.244–256<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Muttering over the announced results on the beach, then named through the lounge retelling as the cautious holder of the Class A cave.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Something is strange… What does this mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class A takes third with 120 points, behind Class B’s 140 and Class D’s 225.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question follows the narration that he muttered it; recorded as his. The Class A cry “What’s the meaning of this, Katsuragi?!” comes from unnamed voices and is left out as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The one who read his cave display as insurance rather than carelessness — the leader beside him was Yahiko, not him.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Totsuka Yahiko was Class A’s leader; Katsuragi only displayed the card while the two were at the cave.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Class A’s internal schism is the reason Katsuragi could not rely on other people — why the methods revealed Class A so easily.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> The retelling’s reading of his class: 270 points at the end of the test, not one spent — bought through Class C’s sacrifice — and still third, Ayanokōji’s own label for it intuition with no evidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p222-1\">← Before: Ch.6 §6.9: the handshake in the woods<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kanzaki-ryuuji ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 2  2 5  the class a pivot on horikita at the 20 40 gathering he singles horikita out of the line  then holds court against her  kanzaki  and ryuen   unless i m mistaken  you re also in the group meeting at 20 40  yes   that s good news  i wanted to speak with you again  i m also in the 20 40 group  starting tomorrow  we will be working together   you re correct  i certainly haven t acknowledged anyone in class d until now  however  considering the incredible results from the last test  it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you  wouldn t you agree  you laid the groundwork to win  and succeeded handsomely   i don t know what the future might hold  but should class d overtake class c  know that class a would attack you without mercy   that s certainly true  however  we must be cautious  it s no laughing matter when those who have been perceived as weak and stupid begin to rise up  if one class manages to change its station  we must be vigilant  i would give the same warning to both classes b and c   however  just because you got lucky and won by complete chance doesn t make us equals   anyone could accomplish something like that out of pure luck  it s better that you don t grow arrogant and behave foolishly after a win that came about by chance  remember that the difference in our class points is still massive   that s a rather deplorable thing to say  especially when academic success is the most important factor in determining our futures  you realize that japan is often referred to as an academic society   to ryuen   i won t let you bring your awful attitude to this test   well  it doesn t matter  since we re in the same group now  we ll be able to talk at length   are you okay  hirata  i think this is going to be an especially grueling battle  calm and collected to a degree that reads as college age   most had already acknowledged him as their leader    the class a entourage glares on cue  dismissive gesture  like he was brushing dirt off his clothes  while calling the island win luck  the pivot from island test indifference to a formal class a threat  brushed off by him  then trading academic ability arguments with ryuen in front of him  the  beauty and the beast  provocation and the awful attitude standoff  names him the group s grinding battle ahead","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.5: the Class A pivot on Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–60<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the 20:40 gathering he singles Horikita out of the line, then holds court against her, Kanzaki, and Ryūen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Unless I’m mistaken, you’re also in the group meeting at 20:40, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s good news. I wanted to speak with you again. I’m also in the 20:40 group. Starting tomorrow, we will be working together.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re correct. I certainly haven’t acknowledged anyone in Class D until now. However, considering the incredible results from the last test, it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you. Wouldn’t you agree? You…”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re correct. I certainly haven’t acknowledged anyone in Class D until now. However, considering the incredible results from the last test, it would be impossible for me not to pay attention to you. Wouldn’t you agree? You laid the groundwork to win, and succeeded handsomely.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know what the future might hold, but…should Class D overtake Class C, know that Class A would attack you without mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s certainly true. However, we must be cautious. It’s no laughing matter when those who have been perceived as weak and stupid begin to rise up. If one class manages to change its station, we must be vigilant. I would give the same warning to both Classes B and C.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, just because you got lucky and won by complete chance doesn’t make us equals.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyone could accomplish something like that out of pure luck. It’s better that you don’t grow arrogant and behave foolishly after a win that came about by chance. Remember that the difference in our class points is still massive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a rather deplorable thing to say. Especially when academic success is the most important factor in determining our futures. You realize that Japan is often referred to as an academic society?” (to Ryūen)<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t let you bring your awful attitude to this test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, it doesn’t matter. Since we’re in the same group now, we’ll be able to talk at length.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you okay, Hirata? I think this is going to be an especially grueling battle.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and collected to a degree that reads as college-age; “most had already acknowledged him as their leader” — the Class A entourage glares on cue.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Dismissive gesture “like he was brushing dirt off his clothes” while calling the island win luck.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The pivot from island-test indifference to a formal Class A threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Brushed off by him, then trading academic-ability arguments with Ryūen in front of him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The “Beauty and the Beast” provocation and the awful-attitude standoff.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Names him the group’s grinding battle ahead.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1\">→ After: Ch.3: named as the island strategist and the no-discussion plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru machida-kouji ichinose-honami katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  named as the island strategist and the no discussion plan never in the room this half   he anchors horikita s dragon list  ryuen s cafe autopsy  and the whole rabbit debate as the man whose fairness strategy machida speaks for  first name on horikita s dragon roster   class a  with nishikawa  matoba and yano  ayanokoji s answer to  who are you most wary of  katsuragi is the most excellent first year  ryuuen the one he fears    by a mile  ryuen reports katsuragi was  rather cautious  of horikita after the island  still thinks horikita planned the whole island win  ryuen says katsuragi  probably didn t know  the points flow and that katsuragi  thinks you planned the whole thing  ryuen   neither katsuragi nor ichinose is my enemy  if i wanted to crush them  i could do it any time  the rabbit room learns his proposal by name through machida  don t discuss at all  let the test pass calmly  equal points for every class  the fairness argument machida voices   vips distributed evenly because the school hates unfairness  island proof   is attributed to katsuragi s read of the test s  trick  narration  his plan is the ultimate defensive move  if a vip is in class a  finding them becomes exceptionally difficult  dragon groupmate  worth watching rival  and the island winner he still misreads  the cafe theme   ryuen quotes his caution and his wrong leader call  named as the author of the no discussion strategy  the opponent who names and dismantles the plan in his absence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: named as the island strategist and the no-discussion plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.64–67, p.70–76, p.85–88<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Never in the room this half — he anchors Horikita’s Dragon list, Ryūen’s café autopsy, and the whole Rabbit debate as the man whose fairness strategy Machida speaks for.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> First name on Horikita’s Dragon roster — Class A, with Nishikawa, Matoba and Yano.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Ayanokōji’s answer to “who are you most wary of”: Katsuragi is the most excellent first-year, Ryuuen the one he fears — “by a mile.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Ryūen reports Katsuragi was “rather cautious” of Horikita after the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Still thinks Horikita planned the whole island win; Ryūen says Katsuragi “probably didn’t know” the points flow and that Katsuragi “thinks you planned the whole thing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Ryūen: “Neither Katsuragi nor Ichinose is my enemy. If I wanted to crush them, I could do it any time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The Rabbit room learns his proposal by name through Machida: don’t discuss at all, let the test pass calmly, equal points for every class.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The fairness argument Machida voices — VIPs distributed evenly because the school hates unfairness, island proof — is attributed to Katsuragi’s read of the test’s “trick.”<span class=\"pg\">p.86–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Narration: his plan is the ultimate defensive move; if a VIP is in Class A, finding them becomes exceptionally difficult.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dragon groupmate, worth-watching rival, and the island winner he still misreads.<span class=\"pg\">p.64, 67, 70, 72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The café theme — Ryūen quotes his caution and his wrong leader call.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Named as the author of the no-discussion strategy.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The opponent who names and dismantles the plan in his absence.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5: the Class A pivot on Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p84-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the talent bar and the dismissed plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p84-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  the talent bar and the dismissed plan named as one of the school s few who could match ichinose s talents   then as the strategist whose plan she dismissed without replacing  in the read of ichinose as a de facto leader  not even katsuragi or ryuuen could do the same   and even hirata and kushida might find themselves outmatched  after class a marches out  ichinose s dismissal of katsuragi s strategy leaves no new resolution   the narration wonders what else she hides","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p84-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the talent bar and the dismissed plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.84, p.96<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as one of the school’s few who could match Ichinose’s talents — then as the strategist whose plan she dismissed without replacing.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> In the read of Ichinose as a de facto leader, not even Katsuragi or Ryuuen could do the same — and even Hirata and Kushida might find themselves outmatched.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> After Class A marches out, Ichinose’s dismissal of Katsuragi’s strategy leaves no new resolution — the narration wonders what else she hides.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p64-1\">← Before: Ch.3: named as the island strategist and the no-discussion plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the calm image and the surprise reaction<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"machida-kouji kouenji-rokusuke katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  the calm image and the surprise reaction still not in the room   his maintained image runs class a s second gathering phones  and his name surfaces when kouenji ends a group   i thought their loss during the test on the island would ve changed them  but katsuragi had them maintaining their calm   image  it was an exceptionally effective strategy  named with ryuen and ichinose as the leaders who  would all be surprised  by kouenji s early traitor move    probably no one had imagined that someone would turn traitor so soon  the front man keeping the calm class a image  one of the three the monkey exit blindsides","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the calm image and the surprise reaction<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.106, p.115<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Still not in the room — his maintained image runs Class A’s second-gathering phones, and his name surfaces when Kouenji ends a group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> “I thought their loss during the test on the island would’ve changed them, but Katsuragi had them maintaining their calm … image. It was an exceptionally effective strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106-107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Named with Ryūen and Ichinose as the leaders who “would all be surprised” by Kouenji’s early traitor move — “Probably no one had imagined that someone would turn traitor so soon.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> The front man keeping the calm Class A image.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> One of the three the Monkey exit blindsides.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p84-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the talent bar and the dismissed plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4: support and confrontation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p128-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 4  support and confrontation named as the backup a counter claims ayanokoji lacks   then as the man ichinose means to confront  a counter says he has no support like ichinose san and katsuragi kun do   only enemies  no reliable information  ichinose intends to see the man who devised class a s plan  ayanokoji asks to come along and whether she wants to talk to katsuragi kun too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: support and confrontation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.128, p.139<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named as the backup a counter claims Ayanokōji lacks — then as the man Ichinose means to confront.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A counter says he has no support like Ichinose-san and Katsuragi-kun do — only enemies, no reliable information.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose intends to see the man who devised Class A’s plan; Ayanokōji asks to come along and whether she wants to talk to Katsuragi-kun too.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p106-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the calm image and the surprise reaction<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p140-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the castle gate holds<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p140-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 4  4 1  the castle gate holds leaves the dragon room into ichinose s ambush  refuses to reopen discussion for the fourth time running and walks away with the strategy intact   ichinose  what are you doing here   well  the testing period is three days long  i have several minutes available  doesn t ignore her    looked happy to engage  with class b s leader  waves the other class a students on and stays alone with the pair   that s extremely reasonable  but i ve heard this question so many times that i feel like my ears are going to fall off  unfortunately  ichinose  you ve wasted your time  said katsuragi   the answer will always be the same  i developed that strategy to win  my reasons are good  you think this test requires communication  that s why you don t agree with me  but you re wrong  this test is about thinking  if you miss that  it s a big problem  so  in keeping with the theme of the test  i ve decided to stifle discussion  the no disclosure strategy is re stated as deliberate  thinking over talking  four outcomes  any one of them legitimate   what i ve said might sound bad  but it s not  i m looking out for my class  looking for ways to not only preserve our standing in this test  but in tests to come  do you agree that there s nothing wrong with me protecting my class   any further discussion is meaningless  ichinose  you can t change my mind  he said   do you still intend to fight  asked katsuragi   i m sorry  but the result s a foregone conclusion  if class a doesn t participate  there s not much you can do  there shouldn t be any way for you to win  said katsuragi   i want to ask you one thing  if you were class a s leader  what would you do  wouldn t you implement the same strategy  asked katsuragi   in my opinion  if you were standing in my position  you would ve come up with the same strategy i did  if it s to protect my class  i don t particularly mind being criticized by others  katsuragi locked eyes with ichinose  the immovable object exchange  closes his eyes  crosses his arms  re meets her gaze   no inch given before the exam ends  still the man ichinose came to counter  no mention of ryuuen in this exchange","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4.1: the castle gate holds<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.140–143<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaves the Dragon room into Ichinose’s ambush; refuses to reopen discussion for the fourth time running and walks away with the strategy intact.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ichinose? What are you doing here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, the testing period is three days long. I have several minutes available.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s extremely reasonable. But I’ve heard this question so many times that I feel like my ears are going to fall off. Unfortunately, Ichinose, you’ve wasted your time,” said Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doesn’t ignore her — “looked happy to engage” with Class B’s leader; waves the other Class A students on and stays alone with the pair.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The answer will always be the same. I developed that strategy to win. My reasons are good. You think this test requires communication. That’s why you don’t agree with me, but you’re wrong. This test is about thinking. If you miss that, it’s a big problem. So, in keeping with the theme of the test, I’ve decided to stifle discussion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The no-disclosure strategy is re-stated as deliberate: thinking over talking, four outcomes, any one of them legitimate.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What I’ve said might sound bad, but it’s not. I’m looking out for my class, looking for ways to not only preserve our standing in this test, but in tests to come. Do you agree that there’s nothing wrong with me protecting my class?”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Any further discussion is meaningless, Ichinose. You can’t change my mind,” he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you still intend to fight?” asked Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but the result’s a foregone conclusion. If Class A doesn’t participate, there’s not much you can do. There shouldn’t be any way for you to win,” said Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I want to ask you one thing. If you were Class A’s leader, what would you do? Wouldn’t you implement the same strategy?” asked Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In my opinion, if you were standing in my position, you would’ve come up with the same strategy I did. If it’s to protect my class, I don’t particularly mind being criticized by others.” Katsuragi locked eyes with Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The immovable-object exchange; closes his eyes, crosses his arms, re-meets her gaze — no inch given before the exam ends.<span class=\"pg\">p.140-143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Still the man Ichinose came to counter; no mention of Ryuuen in this exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4: support and confrontation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p146-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the fortress read<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p146-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 4  the fortress read named through the corridor strategy talk as the man with his own plan  just as katsuragi had his own strategy  ryuuen had come up with a very ryuuen like plan   things were evolving  ryuuen asks whether katsuragi will cooperate  the narration calls him most definitely cautious  one who probably wouldn t move without evidence  kanzaki reports katsuragi is completely unapproachable   he ll talk but won t give an inch  the real problem is called his iron fortress strategy  class a is said to be split into two factions  one led by katsuragi and one by sakayanagi  morishige turned against katsuragi on the island test  the contrast  ichinose wants open  honest conversation to narrow the suspects  while katsuragi aimed for stability by suppressing all conversation  narration  katsuragi had been rather thorough in carrying out his plan","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p146-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the fortress read<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.146, p.148, p.150, p.158–159, p.184<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named through the corridor strategy talk as the man with his own plan.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Just as Katsuragi had his own strategy, Ryuuen had come up with a very Ryuuen-like plan — things were evolving.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen asks whether Katsuragi will cooperate; the narration calls him most definitely cautious, one who probably wouldn’t move without evidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kanzaki reports Katsuragi is completely unapproachable — he’ll talk but won’t give an inch; the real problem is called his iron fortress strategy.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Class A is said to be split into two factions, one led by Katsuragi and one by Sakayanagi; Morishige turned against Katsuragi on the island test.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The contrast: Ichinose wants open, honest conversation to narrow the suspects, while Katsuragi aimed for stability by suppressing all conversation.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Narration: Katsuragi had been rather thorough in carrying out his plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p140-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the castle gate holds<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.0: the iron fortress still running<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p205-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 5  5 0  the iron fortress still running named in the final day opening as the unchanged half of the stalemate   no counter to ichinose s cards  strategy unbroken  the pair of strategies the narration sets against ichinose s missing countermeasure   frontal assault versus iron fortress  still no counter from class b to his silence  that is why cards win the hour  no scene presence in this half  the row records the opening status line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.0: the iron fortress still running<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.205<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the final-day opening as the unchanged half of the stalemate — no counter to Ichinose’s cards, strategy unbroken.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The pair of strategies the narration sets against Ichinose’s missing countermeasure — frontal assault versus iron fortress.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Still no counter from Class B to his silence; that is why cards win the hour.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence in this half; the row records the opening status line.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p146-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the fortress read<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p226-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: instructions, faction, the defensive vote<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p226-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"machida-kouji morishige-takurou sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 5  5 2 5 3  instructions  faction  the defensive vote the chain machida cites  the plan morishige was expected to disobey  and the defensive player example in ayanokoji s dragon outcome  1 explanation   we ve been acting on katsuragi san s instructions from the very beginning    class a s no  line  ichinose s read  he would not quietly sit on katsuragi s plan   sakayanagi faction first  the faction morishige answers to  not katsuragi  the defensive vote ryuuen bent  even katsuragi could vote in the riskless half hour on a 1  kushida seed  the seed question that would have convinced his bloc  no scene presence  three mention anchors only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p226-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 §5.2–5.3: instructions, faction, the defensive vote<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.226, 233, 242<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The chain Machida cites, the plan Morishige was expected to disobey, and the defensive-player example in Ayanokōji’s Dragon Outcome #1 explanation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"morishige-takurou.html\">Morishige Takurō<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> “We’ve been acting on Katsuragi-san’s instructions from the very beginning” — Class A’s no自主 line.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishige Takurō<\/b> Ichinose’s read: he would not quietly sit on Katsuragi’s plan — Sakayanagi faction first.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> The faction Morishige answers to, not Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The defensive vote Ryuuen bent: even Katsuragi could vote in the riskless half hour on a 1% Kushida seed.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The seed question that would have convinced his bloc.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> No scene presence; three mention anchors only.<span class=\"pg\">p.226-242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.5 §5.0: the iron fortress still running<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p48-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 2  the man at the doors at the opened elevator  katsuragi  anxious beyond his size  having taken ayanokoji s cut off call and moved the car by remote   are you all right  ayanokouji  the large man asked  mutual thanks  he took the dying call  praises the plan he proposed despite resistance  and offers help    i ll assist you with anything other than exams  of course   sudou performed brilliantly    asked to be told once again that he is very appreciative  the friendship is treated as established  close as ayanokoji is to the three idiots  maybe more so   and the story of it began a little while ago","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the man at the doors<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.48<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the opened elevator: Katsuragi, anxious beyond his size, having taken Ayanokōji’s cut-off call and moved the car by remote.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you all right, Ayanokouji?” the large man asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Mutual thanks: he took the dying call, praises the plan he proposed despite resistance, and offers help — “I’ll assist you with anything…other than exams, of course.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Sudou performed brilliantly.” — asked to be told once again that he is very appreciative.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The friendship is treated as established: close as Ayanokōji is to the three idiots, maybe more so — and the story of it began a little while ago.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p55-1\">→ After: Ch.3: watched in the girls&#x27; shop<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p55-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  watched in the girls  shop class a s leader browses a pink girls  shop alone  hesitating over thin boxes while three class d boys hide and watch  his forbidding appearance contrasts with the store  he looks around as if worried   but only about the choice  ike reads the hesitation correctly  katsuragi does not want anyone to see what he is buying   the birthday is august 29  he buys chocolate with a birthday card  the recipient stays off the page","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: watched in the girls&#x27; shop<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.55–58<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class A&#x27;s leader browses a pink girls&#x27; shop alone, hesitating over thin boxes while three Class D boys hide and watch.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“The birthday is August 29.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His forbidding appearance contrasts with the store; he looks around as if worried — but only about the choice.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Ike reads the hesitation correctly: Katsuragi does not want anyone to see what he is buying.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> He buys chocolate with a birthday card; the recipient stays off the page.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p48-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the man at the doors<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p61-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the illness behind the jokes<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p61-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  the illness behind the jokes kushida tells the room katsuragi lost his hair completely when he was young  due to illness   katsuragi kun lost his hair completely when he was young  due to illness  the fact lands only through kushida  katsuragi is not in the room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p61-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the illness behind the jokes<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.61<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Katsuragi-kun lost his hair completely when he was young, due to illness.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida tells the room Katsuragi lost his hair completely when he was young, due to illness.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The fact lands only through Kushida; Katsuragi is not in the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p55-1\">← Before: Ch.3: watched in the girls&#x27; shop<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p62-1\">→ After: Ch.3: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p62-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  passing mentions the gift hunt keeps him in view from every side  his taste  his possible girlfriend  and his shopping  the group resolves to locate his girlfriend at any cost  other candidates for his present are weighed  the pairing theory turns on him  and ike whines about the idea of katsuragi beating him  sudou s interference plan circulates  and kushida offers his contact information  ayanokoji decides against contacting him directly  he is tailed through the building in his uniform  he is named among the people worth approaching first  the tail waits for him to move  ayanokoji opens the katsuragi case with ike  his specific purchase is contrasted with the assumptions around it  the group rejudges him  the present looked genuine  a celebration in his name is raised  kushida offers to help with his present","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p62-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.62–67, 72–73, 79–83<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The gift hunt keeps him in view from every side: his taste, his possible girlfriend, and his shopping.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The group resolves to locate his girlfriend at any cost.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Other candidates for his present are weighed.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The pairing theory turns on him, and Ike whines about the idea of Katsuragi beating him.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sudou&#x27;s interference plan circulates, and Kushida offers his contact information.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji decides against contacting him directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He is tailed through the building in his uniform.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He is named among the people worth approaching first.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The tail waits for him to move.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji opens the Katsuragi case with Ike.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His specific purchase is contrasted with the assumptions around it.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The group rejudges him: the present looked genuine.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A celebration in his name is raised.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida offers to help with his present.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p61-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the illness behind the jokes<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p74-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the man at the chocolate shelves<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p74-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  the man at the chocolate shelves still in uniform  katsuragi enters the school building  then reappears at the mall with his gift bag un given  he helps ak clean up the chocolate avalanche without a hint of dislike   what are you doing   two are better than one  ak judges him a good guy   the island corn goodwill is the reference   are you giving your girlfriend a present   one of the boxes of chocolates   you re required to wear your uniform if you enter the school   uh  well  i ve various private matters to attend to  he raises the outside contact ban as the school s shared disadvantage  ak privately counts it an advantage   the stipulation that you can t contact anyone on the outside   don t you want to contact your parents or siblings  he asks whether ak is close with horikita  ak explains the forced seating partnership   you re close with horikita  aren t you  third visit to the same store  he agonizes over decisions when someone s feelings are involved   to tell you the truth  this is the third time i ve visited this store   is it strange to celebrate someone s birthday   it s personal  he refuses to name the recipient  and the chapter s first half closes with the school building and store return mysteries open","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p74-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the man at the chocolate shelves<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.74–78<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Still in uniform, Katsuragi enters the school building, then reappears at the mall with his gift bag un-given.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What are you doing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Two are better than one.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you giving your girlfriend a present?”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He helps AK clean up the chocolate avalanche without a hint of dislike.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK judges him a good guy — the island corn goodwill is the reference.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “One of the boxes of chocolates.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re required to wear your uniform if you enter the school,”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Uh, well, I’ve various private matters to attend to,”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> He raises the outside-contact ban as the school&#x27;s shared disadvantage; AK privately counts it an advantage.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The stipulation that you can’t contact anyone on the outside,”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you want to contact your parents or siblings?”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He asks whether AK is close with Horikita; AK explains the forced seating partnership.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re close with Horikita, aren’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Third visit to the same store: he agonizes over decisions when someone&#x27;s feelings are involved.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To tell you the truth, this is the third time I’ve visited this store.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it strange to celebrate someone’s birthday?”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s personal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> He refuses to name the recipient, and the chapter&#x27;s first half closes with the school-building and store-return mysteries open.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p62-1\">← Before: Ch.3: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p88-1\">→ After: Ch.3: ambushed, then at the council desk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p88-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji horikita-manabu katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  ambushed  then at the council desk surrounded by class d on his birthday  he stays guarded   a trap is his first read of class d   what s going on   if you have an ulterior motive  please tell me   well  yes  but i m surprised you found out  ike s uniform question puts him into battle mode  ak s explanation defuses it   how did you know i ve been wearing my uniform   nothing to do with you  he reveals the student council errand and invites ak along once ak name drops the president   i have some business with the student council   you re an acquaintance of his  his request  one sided package and message to family  refused even as one sided   i d like to send a package and message to my family off campus   this school is all about fostering one s abilities  the points argument gets him the question of recipient   and the twin sister reveal   since we re orphans  i m the only one who celebrates her birthday  twin sister  orphans  he is the only one who marks her birthday  final refusal  rules cannot be bought off with points  he leaves with a glance at ak   well then  if you ll please excuse me","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p88-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: ambushed, then at the council desk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.88–94<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Surrounded by Class D on his birthday, he stays guarded — a trap is his first read of Class D.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../world/student-council-room.html\">Student Council Room<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What’s going on?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you have an ulterior motive, please tell me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, yes, but…I’m surprised you found out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Ike&#x27;s uniform question puts him into battle mode; AK&#x27;s explanation defuses it.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How did you know I’ve been wearing my uniform?”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nothing to do with you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> He reveals the student council errand and invites AK along once AK name-drops the president.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have some business with the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re an acquaintance of his?”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> His request: one-sided package and message to family; refused even as one-sided.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like to send a package and message to my family off-campus.”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This school is all about fostering one’s abilities.”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The points argument gets him the question of recipient — and the twin sister reveal.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since we’re orphans, I’m the only one who celebrates her birthday,”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Twin sister; orphans; he is the only one who marks her birthday.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Final refusal: rules cannot be bought off with points; he leaves with a glance at AK.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, if you’ll please excuse me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p74-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the man at the chocolate shelves<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p95-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the lobby defeat and the room plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p95-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  the lobby defeat and the room plan back in the lobby  depressed  he offers ak the gift  ak refuses and counters with a plan   i don t really care for sweets   it was hopeless  anyway   i can t imagine there s a solution   i m not going to do something that risky  in ak s spartan room he works the problem aloud  employees are regulated  leaving means expulsion   you have quite a clean room   club tournaments  hmm  he reasons out the tournament exception and the bag inspection problem himself   there will be bag inspections   however  judging by what you ve said  ayanokouji  you have a talented  trustworthy individual in mind","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the lobby defeat and the room plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.95–97<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back in the lobby, depressed, he offers AK the gift; AK refuses and counters with a plan. In AK&#x27;s spartan room he works the problem aloud: employees are regulated, leaving means expulsion.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t really care for sweets,”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It was hopeless, anyway,”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I can’t imagine there’s a solution.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not going to do something that risky,”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You have quite a clean room.”<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Club tournaments, hmm?”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He reasons out the tournament exception and the bag-inspection problem himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There will be bag inspections,”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, judging by what you’ve said, Ayanokouji, you have a talented, trustworthy individual in mind.”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p88-1\">← Before: Ch.3: ambushed, then at the council desk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p98-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the contract with Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p98-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  the contract with sudou he and ak pitch sudou after club  sudou s first answer is a flat refusal  sudou s inspection knowledge is what makes the plan concrete   i ll pay you 100 000 points if you succeed  the twin sister story   sickly  relatives caring  parents and grandparents gone   is told to sudou   because our parents and grandparents have passed  our relatives currently care for her   if i don t celebrate her birthday  who will  20 000 advance  80 000 on completion   the advance binds both parties  payment routes through ak  proof is a video from ak s phone hidden in the water bottle   i want ironclad proof you aren t lying to me   i d like you to record a video the moment you send the package  ak s fee  10 000 points for carrying the phone  sudou delivers  whether the sister received it stays unknown to ak","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p98-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the contract with Sudou<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.98–104<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He and AK pitch Sudou after club; Sudou&#x27;s first answer is a flat refusal.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll pay you 100,000 points if you succeed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Because our parents and grandparents have passed, our relatives currently care for her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If I don’t celebrate her birthday, who will?”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou&#x27;s inspection knowledge is what makes the plan concrete.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The twin-sister story — sickly, relatives caring, parents and grandparents gone — is told to Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> 20,000 advance, 80,000 on completion — the advance binds both parties.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Payment routes through AK; proof is a video from AK&#x27;s phone hidden in the water bottle.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I want ironclad proof you aren’t lying to me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like you to record a video the moment you send the package.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> AK&#x27;s fee: 10,000 points for carrying the phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou delivers; whether the sister received it stays unknown to AK.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p95-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the lobby defeat and the room plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the birthday from his side<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p105-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 3  the birthday from his side from katsuragi s viewpoint  two class d boys wait outside his floor and hit him with party poppers   what are you doing   you don t have any reason to   b but i can t accept  he flinches at ike s vulgar language and ends up holding the box anyway   they said it was a cake  but it s actually rather warm   is this some new form of harassment  he imagines the melted ice cream cake as a new form of harassment   and the chapter ends on his read","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the birthday from his side<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.105–106<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">From Katsuragi&#x27;s viewpoint: two Class D boys wait outside his floor and hit him with party poppers.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What are you doing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You don’t have any reason to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“B-but I can’t accept…”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> He flinches at Ike&#x27;s vulgar language and ends up holding the box anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “They said it was a cake, but it’s actually rather warm,”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is this some new form of harassment?”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He imagines the melted ice cream cake as a new form of harassment — and the chapter ends on his read.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p98-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the contract with Sudou<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p121-1\">→ After: Ch.4: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p121-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 4  a passing mention ayanokoji guesses the water thief was ryuen or katsuragi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.121<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji guesses the water thief was Ryūen or Katsuragi.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p105-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the birthday from his side<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p122-1\">→ After: Ch.4: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p122-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 4  a passing mention named with ryuuen as ak s private guess for who steered the ship exam outcome  the speculation is ak s alone  no evidence is offered either way","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p122-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.122<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named with Ryuuen as AK&#x27;s private guess for who steered the ship-exam outcome.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> The speculation is AK&#x27;s alone; no evidence is offered either way.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p121-1\">← Before: Ch.4: a passing mention<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p174-1\">→ After: Ch.6: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p174-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 6  a passing mention ak credits the funds from him for buying the rash guard  the funds and the thanks point at katsuragi s payment in the ch3 delivery run","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p174-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.174<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">AK credits the funds from him for buying the rash guard.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> The funds and the thanks point at Katsuragi&#x27;s payment in the ch3 delivery run.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v4_5-p122-1\">← Before: Ch.4: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p26-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru sakayanagi-arisu totsuka-yahiko katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 2  2 2  the class a face assembles the first year class a students in droves after fujimaki s speech and becomes the class s negotiating face at the red team meeting   i hope we can join forces without any problems  strikes the keep out of each other s way pact with hirata   no shared competition details  only a meeting to come for the group events   i was thinking that it d be best if we just keep out of each other s way   letting that information slip might lead to unnecessary conflict down the road   i ll consult with everyone else  warns horikita off him  he ll laugh while he attacks in the same instant   and leaves his own experience unspoken   don t underestimate ryuuen   i ve warned you  introduces sakayanagi by name and asks for sensitivity  watches her quietly while nearly all the class sits with her faction   that s sakayanagi arisu  yahiko is named among the few boys and girls sitting on his side of the line  the narration reads his faction as possibly no longer superior   sakayanagi may be demonstrating her power deliberately","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.2: the Class A face<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.26–31<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Assembles the first-year Class A students in droves after Fujimaki’s speech and becomes the class’s negotiating face at the Red Team meeting.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I hope we can join forces without any problems,”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I was thinking that it’d be best if we just keep out of each other’s way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Letting that information slip might lead to unnecessary conflict down the road.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Strikes the keep-out-of-each-other’s-way pact with Hirata — no shared competition details, only a meeting to come for the group events.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll consult with everyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Warns Horikita off him: he’ll laugh while he attacks in the same instant — and leaves his own experience unspoken.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t underestimate Ryuuen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve warned you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Introduces Sakayanagi by name and asks for sensitivity; watches her quietly while nearly all the class sits with her faction.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s Sakayanagi Arisu.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Yahiko is named among the few boys and girls sitting on his side of the line.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The narration reads his faction as possibly no longer superior — Sakayanagi may be demonstrating her power deliberately.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4: The standing Class A meetings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru katsuragi-kouhei","q":"katsuragi kohei ch 4  4  the standing class a meetings katsuragi is named as hirata s periodic counterpart on how the two classes should compete  meetings continue through the run up   class d  an inch from disaster  is doing almost too well  background  ryuuen refused to cooperate with class b earlier in the volume  so no class c b channel exists","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 §4: The standing Class A meetings<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Katsuragi is named as Hirata’s periodic counterpart on how the two classes should compete.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Meetings continue through the run-up — Class D, an inch from disaster, is doing almost too well.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Background: Ryuuen refused to cooperate with Class B earlier in the volume, so no Class C–B channel exists.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v5-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: the Class A face<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
